Reason: ov5647_init_controls() calls v4l2_get_subdevdata() to access the i2c_client, but the subdev data is only set by v4l2_i2c_subdev_init() later in the probe. When an error occurs inside init_controls(), the code attempts to use the uninitialized subdev data, which leads to a NULL pointer dereference (segfault) in functions like dev_err that rely on the client pointer.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```
v4l2_i2c_subdev_init(sd, client, &ov5647_subdev_ops);
...
ret = ov5647_init_controls(sensor);
if (ret)
    goto mutex_destroy;
```
Reason: By moving ov5644_init_controls() after v4l2_i2c_subdev_init(), the subdev data (including the i2c_client pointer) is properly initialized before it is accessed in init_controls(). This prevents the NULL pointer dereference that occurred when error handling invoked v4l2_get_subdevdata() on an uninitialized structure.

